**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. Define the detector noise data required by 001 §I without moving the bench implementation before 001 §Q / §S10. In OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs, after ParameterName and DialSign from step 205: `ParameterValue of double` with `.value`, one parameter's number in its kind's unit. `ParameterKind` = `AngleParameter` (radians: an azimuth, an axis or dial offset, an ellipticity angle, a rotation uncertainty) | `PhaseParameter` (radians: a retardance) | `FractionParameter` (dimensionless in [0, 1]: an extinction ratio, a diattenuation, a degree of polarization, an element or throughput uncertainty) | `ScaleParameter` (a dimensionless multiplier: an intensity scale, a gain) | `MuellerElementParameter` (one Mueller-matrix element) | `ThicknessParameter` (metres) | `ReadingParameter` (a detector reading in its own units: a dark offset). `ItemParameterAxis = { name : ParameterName; kind : ParameterKind; defaultValue : ParameterValue }` is one parameter a model publishes. Detector model files store their axis descriptors, so ParameterKind MUST carry stable integer wire tags 1 through 7 in the declaration order above and tryOfWire : int -> ParameterKind option, with zero and unrecognized tags returning None. Its text rendering MUST remain separate from its tag. On ItemParameterAxis, declare static member detectorNoiseAxes (rotation : ParameterValue) (element : ParameterValue) (throughput : ParameterValue) : ItemParameterAxis list. It MUST return rotationUncertainty with AngleParameter, then elementUncertainty and throughputUncertainty with FractionParameter, preserving the supplied values. A detector model MUST carry that ItemParameterAxis list; an instantiated item carries the corresponding ordinary Parameter states. Domain MUST NOT declare or reference AngleUncertainty, ElementUncertainty, ThroughputUncertainty or NoiseParam. Their sole declarations MUST remain in Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs until step 339 moves all four to Optimization/BenchNoise.fs. No new noise-budget record, duplicated bench constants, dependency from Domain to Optimization, or product reference to a test assembly is permitted. In ItemModelsTests, add `the detector noise axes keep their declared quantities`: construct elevated test-local rotation, element and throughput values (0.001 radians, 0.02 and 0.03), call detectorNoiseAxes, and assert names, kinds, order and exact defaults. This data-projection test MUST NOT claim to test a promoted bench model. The axis fact MUST verify every ParameterKind tag round-trips and that zero and an unrecognized tag return None.

**Acceptance.** After detector noise axes are defined, Domain MUST publish the three named axes with the supplied values, without declaring any bench-noise type; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass including `the detector noise axes keep their declared quantities`, the count rising by 1; build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
